spoint STARTUP 5fps FIX (gm-skill 2026-06-18, branch dna-quality-fixes, commit 6aee0a20 pushed). User: 'at start we get 5fps while the assets add one by one, sort them all out before drawing a frame'. ROOT: client/app.js _finishLoading() called loadingScreen.hide() FIRST, then setTimeout(800) built terrain->vegetation->rocks; createVegetation (client/core/Vegetation.js) builds 5 species ONE-per-rAF each baking a 1024^2 octahedral impostor atlas (8x8 MRT views) + meshopt LOD simplify - multi-second GPU stalls that ran AFTER the curtain lifted = the visible 5fps add-in. FIX: new app.js _buildWorldScenery() = await createTerrainBackdrop + Promise.all([_ensureVegetation,_ensureRocks]) (both now RETURN their build promises; createVegetation resolves only after all species+impostor bakes done); _finishLoading awaits it BEHIND the curtain (label 'Preparing terrain...') then loadingScreen.hide(). Bounded by Promise.race timeout (20s singleplayer / 12s MP) so a slow/failed bake still reveals (P9 no silent hang; on timeout the remainder finishes post-reveal = the old behaviour, never worse). The animate rAF loop runs during the await so the per-species rAF-yielding bakes progress. WITNESS (singleplayer localhost:3001): during build loadingDisplay flex/block (curtain held ~25s cold); at reveal impostors=5 + totalInstances 2633 + hasTerrain true (all built behind curtain) and post-reveal fps=56 (NOT 5), #loading-screen gone, no pageErr. Resolved startup-gate-first-frame + startup-lag-since-trees. NOTE the curtain is up longer on cold load (worker boot + assets + scenery build incl 5 bakes ~20-30s) - acceptable per user 'sort them all out before drawing a frame'; the warm-cache reload is much faster. If reveal feels too long later, the lever is faster/cached impostor bakes (offline pre-bake committed atlases) not un-gating.